  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-29T06:14:42.933Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If a gameobject isn't attached to the humanoid armature's hips (via either weight or parenting), it will move several times farther than the player does in-game. The bug seems to be local-only (I asked and others said the object did not travel away).\nOnly happens if:\n- The user is in FBT\n- The avatar is humanoid\n- The bone or gameobject is not weighted or a descendent of the humanoid's armature object\n- \"Force Locomotion animations for 6 point tracking\" is disabled\nTo reproduce:\n- Make a humanoid 3.0 avatar.\n- Add a default cube as a child of the avatar descriptor object\n- Set \"Force Locomotion animations for 6 point tracking\" to disabled\n- Log into vrchat with full-body tracking and calibrate the avatar\n- Move using the trackpad\nYou will see the cube move separately from you\n\nEDIT: A workaround is to set the object as a direct child of the Armature. The bug only seems to happen to objects that aren't descendents of the Armature. This seems to reduce the glitching, but not totally remove it.\nEDIT 2: The issue only happens when \"Force Locomotion animations for 6 point tracking\" is disabled",
